5. Thermodynamic Consistency

5.1 Gradient Structure on the Reaction Term

Hypothesis (H-TH). There exists a convex functional $\mathcal{F}_{\text{BUDT}}: H^1 \to \mathbb{R}$ with $\mathcal{F}_{\text{BUDT}} \in C^1$ such that
F_{\text{BUDT}}(\Psi) = -\nabla_\Psi \mathcal{F}_{\text{BUDT}}(\Psi). \tag{5.1}


Moreover, $\mathcal{F}_{\text{BUDT}}$ has a unique minimizer $\Psi^*$ in $H^1$ and is coercive.

Remark 5.1. (H-TH) is a structural assumption on the active inference term. It holds if the free energy landscape is convex near the NESS, which is the standard assumption in active inference. It may fail far from equilibrium.

5.2 Geometric Decomposition of Entropy Production (Corrected Sign)

Following Nagayama, Yoshimura, Kolchinsky, and Ito, we decompose the entropy production rate as
\sigma = \sigma_{\text{diff}} + \sigma_{\text{react}} + \sigma_{\text{cross}}, \tag{5.2}


where
\sigma_{\text{diff}} = \frac{D}{T} |\nabla \Psi|^2 \ge 0, \tag{5.3}


and the reaction term is defined with the sign convention
\sigma_{\text{react}} = -\frac{1}{T} \left\langle F_{\text{BUDT}}(\Psi) - F_{\text{BUDT}}(\Psi^*), \, \Psi - \Psi^* \right\rangle. \tag{5.4}

Proposition 5.2 (Non-negativity of reaction entropy production; corrected). Under (H-TH) with $\mathcal{F}_{\text{BUDT}}$ convex, $\sigma_{\text{react}} \ge 0$.

Proof. Under (H-TH), $F_{\text{BUDT}}(\Psi) - F_{\text{BUDT}}(\Psi^*) = -\nabla \mathcal{F}(\Psi) + \nabla \mathcal{F}(\Psi^*)$. Therefore
\sigma_{\text{react}} = \frac{1}{T} \left\langle \nabla \mathcal{F}(\Psi) - \nabla \mathcal{F}(\Psi^*), \, \Psi - \Psi^* \right\rangle \ge 0,


using the monotonicity of the gradient of a convex functional. $\square$

Remark 5.3. An earlier formulation wrote $\sigma_{\text{react}} = \frac{1}{T}(F(\Psi) - F(\Psi^*))(\Psi - \Psi^*)$, which is non-positive under (H-TH) and thus contradicts the claimed non-negativity. The sign convention (5.4) fixes this inconsistency.

Remark 5.4. For diffusive systems, the entropy production is sometimes written as $\sigma_{\text{diff}} = (D/T)|\nabla \log \Psi|^2$ when $\Psi > 0$. Under (SA1)–(SA2), the two forms are comparable up to constants.

Remark 5.5 (When (H-TH) fails). If $F_{\text{BUDT}}$ is not a gradient of a convex functional, the reaction entropy production can be negative locally. In that case, the total entropy production may still be non-negative if the diffusion term dominates:
\frac{D}{T} |\nabla \Psi|^2 \ge \left| \sigma_{\text{react}} \right|.


We state this as an additional hypothesis where needed.

5.3 Thermodynamic Trade-off Relations

Nagayama et al. establish:

1. Speed limits. The rate of pattern formation is bounded by $\sqrt{2\sigma}$.
2. Uncertainty relations. The excess entropy production is bounded below by the information content of the pattern.

These give testable predictions for CFC: the rate at which alignment-relevant patterns form cannot exceed the thermodynamic speed limit.

