8. Categorical Compositionality with Alignment

8.1 Alignment-Enriched Kleisli Category

Let $\mathcal{P}$ be the Giry monad on $\mathbf{Meas}$. The Kleisli category $\mathbf{Meas}_{\mathcal{P}}$ has Markov kernels $k: X \to \mathcal{P}(Y)$ as morphisms.

Definition 8.1 (Alignment-enriched module). An alignment-enriched cognitive module is a pair $(k, \alpha)$ where $k: X \to \mathcal{P}(Y)$ is a Markov kernel and $\alpha: X \to \mathbb{R}_{\ge 0}$ is measurable with
D_{\mathrm{KL}}(k(\cdot|x) \| \mathcal{V}_Y) \le \alpha(x) \quad \text{for all } x \in X,


where $\mathcal{V}_Y$ is a reference distribution on $Y$.

Definition 8.2 (Alignment-enriched composition). For modules $(k,\alpha): X \to Y$ and $(\ell,\beta): Y \to Z$, the composite is $(\ell \circ_K k, \gamma)$ where
\gamma(x) = \int_Y \beta(y) \, k(dy|x). \tag{8.1}

8.2 Alignment Composition Theorem

Theorem 8.3 (Alignment composition). If $(k,\alpha): X \to Y$ and $(\ell,\beta): Y \to Z$ are alignment-enriched modules, then the composite $(\ell \circ_K k, \gamma)$ with $\gamma$ given by (8.1) satisfies
D_{\mathrm{KL}}((\ell \circ_K k)(\cdot|x) \| \mathcal{V}_Z) \le \gamma(x)


for all $x \in X$.

Proof. By convexity of the KL divergence in its first argument,
D_{\mathrm{KL}}\!\left( \int_Y \ell(\cdot|y) k(dy|x) \,\Big\|\, \mathcal{V}_Z \right) \le \int_Y D_{\mathrm{KL}}(\ell(\cdot|y) \| \mathcal{V}_Z) \, k(dy|x) \le \int_Y \beta(y) k(dy|x) = \gamma(x). \qquad \square

Remark 8.4. The previous revision used a "chain rule" for KL divergence that is not standard. The correct estimate is the convexity inequality above. The resulting composition bound is strictly stronger: the $\alpha(x)$ term from the previous revision is unnecessary.

Remark 8.5. Measurability of $\gamma$ follows from the measurability of $k$ and $\beta$. The composition is associative by associativity of the Giry monad.

