Appendix D: Thermodynamic Consistency and the Corrected Sign Convention

This appendix documents the sign error in the prior revision's reaction entropy production formula and its correction.

D.1 Gradient Structure Hypothesis (H-TH)

There exists a convex, coercive, $C^1$ functional $\mathcal{F}_{\text{BUDT}}: H^1 \to \mathbb{R}$ with unique minimizer $\Psi^*$ such that
F_{\text{BUDT}}(\Psi) = -\nabla_\Psi \mathcal{F}_{\text{BUDT}}(\Psi). \tag{D.1}

D.2 Corrected Reaction Entropy Production

Definition D.1 (Reaction entropy production). Under (H-TH), define
\sigma_{\text{react}} = -\frac{1}{T} \left\langle F_{\text{BUDT}}(\Psi) - F_{\text{BUDT}}(\Psi^*), \, \Psi - \Psi^* \right\rangle. \tag{D.2}

Proposition D.2 (Non-negativity). Under (H-TH), $\sigma_{\text{react}} \ge 0$.

Proof. Substituting (D.1) into (D.2):
\sigma_{\text{react}} = \frac{1}{T} \left\langle \nabla \mathcal{F}_{\text{BUDT}}(\Psi) - \nabla \mathcal{F}_{\text{BUDT}}(\Psi^*), \, \Psi - \Psi^* \right\rangle. \tag{D.3}

By monotonicity of the gradient of a convex functional,
\left\langle \nabla \mathcal{F}_{\text{BUDT}}(\Psi) - \nabla \mathcal{F}_{\text{BUDT}}(\Psi^*), \, \Psi - \Psi^* \right\rangle \ge 0. \tag{D.4}

Hence $\sigma_{\text{react}} \ge 0$. $\square$

Remark D.3 (Sign error in prior revision). The prior revision displayed
\sigma_{\text{react}} = \frac{1}{T} \left( F_{\text{BUDT}}(\Psi) - F_{\text{BUDT}}(\Psi^*) \right) (\Psi - \Psi^*). \tag{D.5}

Under (H-TH), this equals
-\frac{1}{T} \left\langle \nabla \mathcal{F}_{\text{BUDT}}(\Psi) - \nabla \mathcal{F}_{\text{BUDT}}(\Psi^*), \, \Psi - \Psi^* \right\rangle \le 0, \tag{D.6}

which is non-positive, contradicting the claimed non-negativity. The sign convention (D.2) resolves this inconsistency.

D.3 Total Entropy Production

Definition D.4. The total entropy production rate is
\sigma = \sigma_{\text{diff}} + \sigma_{\text{react}} + \sigma_{\text{cross}}, \tag{D.7}


where
\sigma_{\text{diff}} = \frac{D}{T} |\nabla \Psi|^2 \ge 0, \tag{D.8}


$\sigma_{\text{react}}$ is given by (D.2) (non-negative under (H-TH)), and $\sigma_{\text{cross}}$ vanishes when the thermodynamic forces are orthogonal.

Corollary D.5. Under (H-TH) and the orthogonality of thermodynamic forces ($\sigma_{\text{cross}} = 0$), $\sigma \ge 0$.

