Appendix G: The Kleisli Composition Bound via Jensen's Inequality

This appendix documents the corrected proof of the alignment composition theorem, replacing the prior revision's non-standard "chain rule."

G.1 Setup

Let $\mathcal{P}$ be the Giry monad on $\mathbf{Meas}$. An alignment-enriched cognitive module is a pair $(k, \alpha)$ with $k: X \to \mathcal{P}(Y)$ a Markov kernel and $\alpha: X \to \mathbb{R}_{\ge 0}$ satisfying $D_{\mathrm{KL}}(k(\cdot|x) \| \mathcal{V}_Y) \le \alpha(x)$.

G.2 Composition

Definition G.1. For modules $(k, \alpha): X \to Y$ and $(\ell, \beta): Y \to Z$, the composite is $(\ell \circ_K k, \gamma)$ with
(\ell \circ_K k)(dz|x) = \int_Y \ell(dz|y) \, k(dy|x), \qquad \gamma(x) = \int_Y \beta(y) \, k(dy|x). \tag{G.1}

G.3 Composition Theorem

Theorem G.2 (Alignment composition; corrected). Let $(k, \alpha): X \to Y$ and $(\ell, \beta): Y \to Z$ be alignment-enriched modules. Then for all $x \in X$,
D_{\mathrm{KL}}((\ell \circ_K k)(\cdot|x) \| \mathcal{V}_Z) \le \gamma(x). \tag{G.2}

Proof. Write $q(dz|x) = (\ell \circ_K k)(dz|x) = \int_Y \ell(dz|y) k(dy|x)$. The KL divergence of $q$ with respect to $\mathcal{V}_Z$ is
D_{\mathrm{KL}}(q \| \mathcal{V}_Z) = \int_Z q(z|x) \log\frac{q(z|x)}{\mathcal{V}_Z(z)} \, dz. \tag{G.3}

By Fubini and the definition of $q$,
D_{\mathrm{KL}}(q \| \mathcal{V}_Z) = \int_Z \left( \int_Y \ell(z|y) k(dy|x) \right) \log\frac{\int_Y \ell(z|y') k(dy'|x)}{\mathcal{V}_Z(z)} \, dz. \tag{G.4}

Apply Jensen's inequality to the convex function $u \mapsto u \log(u/\mathcal{V}_Z(z))$ for fixed $z$:
\left( \int_Y \ell(z|y) k(dy|x) \right) \log\frac{\int_Y \ell(z|y') k(dy'|x)}{\mathcal{V}_Z(z)} \le \int_Y \ell(z|y) \log\frac{\ell(z|y)}{\mathcal{V}_Z(z)} \, k(dy|x). \tag{G.5}

Integrating (G.5) over $z$ and applying Fubini:
D_{\mathrm{KL}}(q \| \mathcal{V}_Z) \le \int_Y \left( \int_Z \ell(z|y) \log\frac{\ell(z|y)}{\mathcal{V}_Z(z)} \, dz \right) k(dy|x) = \int_Y D_{\mathrm{KL}}(\ell(\cdot|y) \| \mathcal{V}_Z) \, k(dy|x). \tag{G.6}

By the alignment-enrichment hypothesis on $(\ell, \beta)$, $D_{\mathrm{KL}}(\ell(\cdot|y) \| \mathcal{V}_Z) \le \beta(y)$. Therefore
D_{\mathrm{KL}}(q \| \mathcal{V}_Z) \le \int_Y \beta(y) \, k(dy|x) = \gamma(x). \qquad \square \tag{G.7}

Remark G.3. The prior revision used a "chain rule" for KL divergence that is not standard (KL divergence is not generally multiplicative under composition). The correct estimate is Jensen's inequality (G.5), which yields a strictly stronger bound: the term $\alpha(x)$ appearing in the prior revision's bound is unnecessary, as the alignment of the first module does not enter the composite bound.

