Appendix H: Reputation-Aware Mean-Field Games — Detailed Derivation

This appendix provides a self-contained derivation of the reputation update and the critical adversarial fraction, under the FedMFG framework.

H.1 Microscopic Model

$N$ agents, fraction $\rho$ adversarial. Cooperative agent dynamics:
dX_t^i = a_t^i \, dt + \sqrt{2\nu} \, dW_t^i, \qquad J^i(a^i) = \mathbb{E}\left[ \int_0^T \left( \frac12 \|a_t^i\|^2 + \mathcal{F}(\theta_t^i; o_t) + V(X_t^i, m_t^N) \right) dt \right]. \tag{H.1}

H.2 Reputation Dynamics

r^i_{t+1} = r^i_t + \kappa \left( \cos(a^i_t, \bar{a}_t) - r^i_t \right), \qquad \bar{a}_t = \frac{1}{N} \sum_{j=1}^N a^j_t. \tag{H.2}

Lemma H.1 (Contraction). Under (H.2), for cooperative agents with $\cos(a^i_t, \bar{a}_t) \ge \theta_r$, the reputation converges exponentially to the set $\{r \ge \theta_r\}$:
|r^i_t - \theta_r| \le (1-\kappa)^t |r^i_0 - \theta_r|. \tag{H.3}

Proof. Standard contraction of the affine update. $\square$

H.3 Linearized FP Operator and Spectral Gap

The mean-field FP equation linearized around the NESS $m^*$ is
\partial_t \delta m = \nu \Delta_x \delta m + \kappa \Delta_{\text{hyb}} \delta m - \nabla_x \cdot (m^* \nabla_x \delta u) - \nabla_x \cdot (\delta m \nabla_x u^*). \tag{H.4}

Under uniform ellipticity $D \ge D_{\min}$ and the spectral gap of the hybrid Laplacian $\Delta_{\text{hyb}}$, the linearized operator has spectral gap $\lambda_{\min}(D) > 0$.

H.4 Critical Adversarial Fraction

Proposition H.2 (Critical fraction; conditional on FedMFG). Under the assumptions of Theorem 9.2, the critical adversarial fraction is
\rho_c = \frac12 \left( 1 - \frac{\kappa}{\kappa + \lambda_{\min}(D)} \right). \tag{H.5}

Derivation sketch. The reputation mechanism excludes adversarial agents whose reputation falls below $\theta_r$. The exclusion rate is governed by the contraction rate $\kappa$. The adversarial contribution to the FP source term is bounded by $\rho (1 - \theta_r)$. Balancing this against the spectral gap $\lambda_{\min}(D)$ of the linearized FP operator yields the critical fraction
\rho (1-\theta_r) \le \frac{\lambda_{\min}(D)}{\kappa + \lambda_{\min}(D)} \cdot \frac{1}{2}. \tag{H.6}

Setting $\theta_r = 0$ and rearranging gives (H.5). $\square$

