Appendix N: Summary of the Central Theoretical Advance

The central advance of this revision is the replacement of the previously conjectural sign condition on the fractional Leibniz remainder (Conjecture 3.10 of the prior revision) by the fractional Lyapunov inequality (Theorem A.1, Theorem A.2). This inequality is a known result in the fractional analysis literature (Gomoyunov 2017; Agarwal–Hristova–O'Regan 2023) and states that for convex Lyapunov functionals, the Caputo derivative satisfies the same differential inequality as the classical derivative, up to a non-positive boundary term that is intrinsic to convexity.

The consequences are:

1. Alignment Invariance (Proposition 3.6) is unconditional under (SA1)–(SA4), the alignment-compatibility condition (3.6), and the dissipativity of the projection term.
2. Hypothesis (H-AI) is eliminated. The prior revision's requirement of an a priori differential inequality on $\mathcal{A}$ is now a theorem.
3. Coherence Preservation (Theorem 10.3) is unconditional under (SA1)–(SA4).
4. Coupled System Existence (Theorem 11.2) is unconditional under (SA1)–(SA4) and the Camilli–De Maio hypotheses.
5. The remaining structural assumptions are:
   · (H-TH), the gradient structure on $F_{\text{BUDT}}$ (standard near equilibrium in active inference);
   · (SA3), the bounded-observable dependence of $D$ on $\Psi$;
   · (H-WFR), the well-definedness of the WFR metric on $\mathcal{M}$;
   · the FedMFG citation status for §9;
   · the fractional Barbălat lemma in the Caputo setting for §11.3.

These are clearly identified, stated as explicit hypotheses, and are the subject of the open problems in §12.2.

